  "Name": "Berning1957-Fig8-spacerless-1.75L-Ag600A",
  "Source": "P. H. Berning and A. F. Turner, \"Induced Transmission in Absorbing Films Applied to Band Pass Filter Design,\" J. Opt. Soc. Am. 47, 230-239 (1957). doi:10.1364/JOSA.47.000230 - Text p. 235 design formula; Fig. 8 caption (h_Ag = 0.1098 lambda); indices p. 236",
  "Notes": "Spacerless induced-transmission silver band-pass filter (calculated)\nSpecification: Narrow pass band with maximum transmittance at 546 nm (phi = 90 deg) and low background; stacks designed so the stack alone (referred to air) has R ~86 % and phase ~211 deg at 546 nm\nReported: Fig. 8(a): calculated half-width 3.6 deg of dielectric phase thickness phi (phi = 90 deg at 546 nm); peak T read from plot ~90 % (approximate). The paper's abscissa is dielectric phase thickness, not wavelength.\nNotes: Symmetric design, so order is the same either way. G = glass, n0 = 1.52 (paper: 'n0 = 1.52'). Ag thickness 0.1098 lambda at 546 nm = 59.95 nm (= 2 x 300 A). Calculations assume nondispersive dielectrics and a wavelength-independent Ag characteristic matrix (the Ag phase thickness is held constant); a recomputation with constant Ag index is therefore only an approximation to the plotted phase-thickness curves.\nLayers from Text p. 235 design formula; Fig. 8 caption (h_Ag = 0.1098 lambda); indices p. 236; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nNot checked: the paper reports this design only as plots.",
